<title>USA: SPC cuts US posted crude 75 cts, WTI $20.00.</title>
<headline>SPC cuts US posted crude 75 cts, WTI $20.00.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ashland Inc's Scurlock Permian unit said it lowered the price it will pay for U.S. crude oil by 75 cents, effective today.</p>
<p>The decrease brings the new price for U.S. benchmark grade West Texas Intermediate to $20.00 a barrel and West Texas Sour to $17.75 a barrel.</p>
<p>Light Louisiana sweet crude is now $20.00 and Oklahoma sweet is $20.00.</p>
<p>--New York Energy Desk, +1 212 859 1623</p>
</text>
